Kent Paul Dolan wrote:

> Rogues/thieves are my _very_ favorite class.
>
> What's not to like? They have far and away the most useful starting
> equippage of any class.
...
>
> A lockpick so no hastling with locks on doors or containers, so no broken
> potions from kicking chests open, so also able to be quiet and still
> visit the whole level.

You <gasp> kick open chests?  (Yes, the lockpick is nice -- especially when
you find "Closed for Inventory". However, crude daggers are usually readily
available from very early on, which can be pet BU/C-id'ed and used to #force
chests.)

> A sack from the get-go, so no problems with "won't fit in your knapsack"
> ills, just the usual burdening issues every class has.

I think this is easily the most important one, not just for inventory slot
conservation, but (more importantly IMO) for preserving potions and scrolls
as well. (plus, the minor benefit of knowing right away that any "bag" you
find is special).  It's also really nice to have, say, that wand of make
invisible *inside that bag* if you don't see invis, don't have telepathy or
a blindfold, and there are nymphs around.

I've had more than one game where I've finished sokoban and minetown before
finding a bag of any kind, and it got to the point where I just about would
have wasted a wish on a plain sack if it wasn't just as easy to wish for a
BoH.  I've certainly appreciated the enormous utility of sacks since then.

